 "structural_change": "MU1 (Qwen ROM 4 users) variant of qkd_kvs_ctl (p1-d7af727c1 EARLY_FAIL_SETUP): tile qkd_kvs_ctl from the _mu tile file (OT_KV_MU=1: u_wrn = qkd_kv_static_writer_native_mu #(.MU(1)), per-user KV row[9:8] from TAG epoch[1:0]); same ports / outline / pins as qkd_kvs_ctl @d7af727c1.  ROOT-RST reset landing ON (rst_n, por_n land in 2 registered stages at the face): p1 failed post-place TT WNS -12,487 ps because rst_n (input port) drove 2,731 RESETN pins as ONE unbuffered net (slew 45 ns, recovery -12.6 ns on every sink); the landing gives the port net one sink and repair_design an equal-depth tree from a register.  Reset assert/release +2 ck (scheduled constant).  NEW kit (RTL-BUILD-KV M1, KV-INTEG/KITS-A): generated static tile qkd_kvs_ctl of the KV die (20 children: qkd_kv_cfault_node, qkd_kv_die_cfg, qkd_kv_es_fan_root2_b, qkd_kv_native_programme, qkd_kv_ownership_obs, qkd_kv_static_writer_native, qkd_static_kv_boot_dispatch, qkd_static_kv_boot_observe, qkd_static_kv_layer_programme, qkd_static_kv_ownership_calendar; hard: none), from rtl/qwen_sys/static_kv_die_20261017/qkd_kvs_tiles_hroot_ff_k.sv (sha256 4db849c89d25) by tools/qwen_kv_die/kvs_tile_kits.py; one clock port ck (OT_KV_TILE_KITS).  Faces {'S': 100, 'N': 1647, 'W': 2524, 'E': 2524} pins on 475.2 x 475.2 um (die frame record (1123.2, 172.8) ASSUMED -> this outline for KV-PLAN3).",
